[Music]  hey everyone welcome to another  installment of harry potter theory in  today's video we're going to once again  be covering the newly released second  secrets of dumbledore trailer which has  given us harry potter fans a lot to talk  about i mentioned a few of these  theories in my trailer breakdown video  link in description but i only scratched  the surface of them in that video and  not all of them so today i'm going to be  discussing in more depth five of my  theories pertaining to the trailer let's  get into it number one where is tina  goldstein  okay now we've had two trailers and one  teaser but absolutely no sign of  porpentina goldstein one of the main  protagonists of both fantastic beasts  and where to find them as well as  fantastic beasts the crimes of  grindelwald in the previous two films we  were given a considerable amount of the  american half blood witch and auras  backstory like the fact that she  attended ilvermorny school of witchcraft  and wizardry and the fact that she was  sorted into thunderbird house she's even  the sister of queenie who's still in the  film so it seems highly unusual that she  would be absent from yet another trailer  so what's the deal well my answer is  this tina goldstein fans should rest  easy as porpentina is far too  intertwined into the story to be removed  altogether i can say this with  confidence for a few reasons first of  all queenie goldstein tina's sister is  still a massive part of the plot and  shows up in the trailer on several  occasions  removing her sister for no apparent  reason would be a huge continuity error  and it just wouldn't make sense i don't  think they'd make a critical error like  that  second of all fantastic beasts fans who  are privy to harry potter lore should  already know that tina eventually  becomes the wife of newt scamander who  just so happens to be the main character  of the films we also know that they go  on to have children removing her would  be far too disruptive to the film and  harry potter cannon it would also  invalidate the tension that has been  building between newt and tina in the  films released thus far lastly catherine  waterston who plays tina has been  credited for the role  so where is she  my theory is that tina is hidden in  plain sight that is we've seen her in  every trailer so far we just didn't  realize it tinam is newt's assistant  bunty  now i'm not saying that bunty isn't an  actual person independent from tina she  totally is but what i'm suggesting is  that tina has used apologies potion to  assume the physical form of bunty now  you might be asking why  i think there are a few reasons for this  but the primary motivation for assuming  the form of bunty is that she's less of  a target bunty is a very unassuming  character already close to newt so  hanging around him wouldn't really arise  any suspicion  this effectively allows tina to act in a  more covert fashion and it might also  allow her to avoid unnecessary  interactions with her sister queenie who  has now switched sides in the trailer we  also see bunty acting a bit out of  character looking at newt quite firmly  and saying no one can know everything  not even you there's also the  possibility that since we're further  along in the future tina is pregnant  with newt's child staying out of the way  to avoid danger although i feel like  this one is a bit premature what do you  think number two the blood pact it's  well known that dumbledore and  grindelwald entered into a blood pact  when they were young  a blood pact is a type of magically  binding agreement between two parties  who shared their blood it could be made  by the parties cutting their hands with  their wands and interlacing them and  making the desired oath upon doing this  two glowing drops of blood would raise  from their palms and mingle into one  thereafter a file would take shape  around it enclosing the drop signifying  that the deal was struck and serving as  a physical manifestation of it once made  the file was supposedly impossible to  destroy  in the case of dumbledore and  grindelwald they made an oath never to  fight each other and grindelwald held  the file in his possession as a  safeguard so that dumbledore wouldn't be  able to try and destroy it as long as  the blood pact remained neither man  could attack the other however in the  secret of dumbledore trailer we see the  file containing their blood in  dumbledore's possession it was given to  dumbledore by newt in the previous film  dumbledore is staring at it presumably  figuring out a way to destroy it and  later in that same trailer we see the  two men dumbledore and grindelwald  fighting if they're actually fighting  and this isn't some kind of dream  sequence or out of body experience then  it means that the pact has been broken  we know that dumbledore eventually  defeats grindelwald in an epic jewel but  i hadn't expected them to duel so early  on in the films grindelwald's defeated  in 1945 and this film is supposed to  take place in 1939. so what's the deal  is this occurring in another dimension  does it jump ahead to 1945 is this the  last film or do we still have two more  number three for the greater good  at one point in the trailer we see  dumbledore and grindelwald sitting  across from one another having a rather  intense conversation grindelwald says to  albus rather ominously with or without  you i'll burn down their world  this is a scary line and once again  paints grindelwald with the brush of the  bad guy and bad guy he certainly is  however a line from that same  conversation later on made me think a  little bit staring dumbledore right in  the eyes grindelwald says to him it was  you who said we would reshape the world  to me this is big because it suggested  perhaps grindelwald's plan of  restructuring the world for the greater  good establishing a new world hierarchy  and enslaving muggles was actually the  master plan of albus dumbledore he just  brought grindelwald along for the ride  up to this point we were led to believe  that the two boys co-created everything  even the slogan but what this could  suggest is that dumbledore was the  original diabolical mastermind only  leaving his plans behind and gaining  perspective after the death of his  sister  4. yusuf karma yusuf karma born in 1884  was a french pureblood wizard of  senegalese ancestry his character is  little all over the place in the films  and he's not exactly a good guy but he  doesn't appear to be evil either he's  grey at least from what we can tell so  far when we're first introduced to yusuf  he's hell-bent on killing credence and  that's because he believed credence to  be corvus lestrange the son of corvus  lestrange iv a man who would use the  imperious curse to marry yusuf's mother  he was also acting under an unbreakable  vow imposed by his father that had him  seek revenge by killing the person who  lestrange loved most in the world after  learning that his foul was void due to  corvus already being dead yusuf started  to display a more moral and selfless  side and was not at all tempted by  grindelwald's persuasive speech at the  lestrange mausoleum  at this point gama risks his life to  save nagini from the black fire and then  helps nicola flamel as well as his  former enemies by conjuring purifying  orange flames but in the new trailer i'm  not entirely sure where yusuf's  allegiance lies in some scenes he's with  the good guys he's even on the train  with them but in others he can be seen  standing behind and interacting with  grindelwald as if he is an acolyte of  grindelwald's so what's the deal  provided that there's a scene in the  trailer where grindelwald is using his  wand to extract something from yusuf i'm  willing to bet that he has manipulated  yusuf in some way in order to bring him  over to his side perhaps he offered to  take away yusuf's painful memories from  childhood or maybe he took away the  memories of him allying up with newt and  gang or maybe just maybe use the  imperius curse to bring yusuf under his  control  number 5. the mirror in the trailer we  see who has been revealed to be young at  before dumbledore staring into a mirror  as words begin to form  this scene has been in both trailers so  far  the only problem with this part of the  trailer is that the sentence is  incomplete we're only given a little bit  of it  so what does it say and where do these  words come from this mirror if you  didn't know is of course a two-way  mirror one in a pair of mirrors that are  magically connected  this type of magical artifact allows  people to communicate with each other  while in different locations immediately  after seeing amber forth it cuts to  albus so clearly the two are using  mirrors to communicate what message did  albus send to his brother  all i can make out is do you know the  top with the standalone sections of w h  i s and i k e  at the bottom it also looks like there's  a question mark at the end of the  sentence i spoke with one who helps run  harry potter theory espanol today and he  seemed to think that it might say  do you know what it's like this would  effectively be dropping an emotional  bomb onto his brother which could make  sense given that aberforth blames him  for so much  however it's also possible that this  text isn't significant at all  later in life albus says the following  of his brother  of course i'm not entirely sure he can  read it sounds like a joke but maybe  there's some truth to it who knows what  do you guys think it says i'd love to  hear what you think and that's it for  this video if you enjoyed the content  please like the video and subscribe to  support the channel  until next time remember  it does not do to dwell on dreams and  forget to live  you

